PREFIX amp: <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/ash-manufacture-pack#>

# The version scope every citation's line numbers are valid at.
#
# This exists as a gate, not only as a checker input, because the scope used
# to live in a `#` comment above the capability instances. A comment cannot be
# projected, cannot be hashed into the receipt, and cannot disagree with
# mix.lock loudly enough for anyone to notice -- the comment named three deps
# while the file cited four.
#
# NO AGGREGATE, and that is a measured decision rather than a stylistic one.
# An earlier revision selected `(COUNT(?cite) AS ?citation_count)` with a
# GROUP BY. Under the oxigraph NIF that returned the right 4 rows. Under the
# DEFAULT engine (`sparql` hex 0.3.12, GgenIgniter.Query.run/2) it returned 41
# rows -- one per citation, GROUP BY silently ignored -- with citation_count
# bound to a nested SPARQL.Query.Result struct instead of an integer. It did
# not raise. A gate that returns confidently wrong rows on the engine that
# actually renders the pack is the fail-open shape this pack is trying to
# remove, so the aggregate is gone. Per-pin citation counts belong to
# bin/citation_check.py, which computes them against real files.
SELECT ?pinned_dep ?pinned_version
WHERE {
  ?pin a amp:DependencyPin ;
       amp:pinnedDep ?pinned_dep ;
       amp:pinnedVersion ?pinned_version .
}
ORDER BY ?pinned_dep
